# Catppuccin Mocha is BUILT IN, so no theme file or `bat cache --build` step is needed.
#
# Recorded because it looks like it should need one. bat historically required Catppuccin
# themes to be dropped into ~/.config/bat/themes/ and compiled, and a review of this file
# flagged the missing themes/ directory as a silent-fallback bug of the ADR-030 class —
# where the terminal looks almost right and nothing reports the difference. It is not:
# `bat --list-themes` on a machine provisioned by this repository lists all four Catppuccin
# variants (Frappe, Latte, Macchiato, Mocha), shipped with bat since 0.26.0.
#
# If a future bat drops them, the symptom is silent: bat falls back to its default theme
# rather than erroring. Check with `bat --list-themes | grep -i catppuccin`.
--theme="Catppuccin Mocha"
--style="numbers,changes,header"
--paging=auto
--italic-text=always
